    "joint_mass": "J(h,b,y) supplied directly, sums to probability_scale exactly",
    "robust_possibility": "physical_branch_observation_pairs are checked independently of joint mass; zero-mass physical branches remain in robust admission",
    "decision": "for each outcome, minimize unnormalized joint expected loss only over that outcome's robust_admitted_action_ids",
    "resources": "hard resource feasibility is checked before decision ranking",
    "unknown": "unknown outcome mass retained; only the named fallback action may be selected",
    "joint_support": "An explicit possibility relation over (hypothesis, physical branch, observation) is supplied separately from probability mass. Its (hypothesis, branch) projection must equal the declared hypothesis-branch support and its (branch, observation) projection must equal the physical branch-observation support. Positive mass outside this exact triple relation is invalid, even when both pairwise projections are individually allowed."
